From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:19:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tccasm: assemble the Linux kernel's .S files (GNU as
 compatibility)

The kernel's x86 assembly is written for GNU as and its macro facility;
to assemble it unchanged:

* Macro bodies and invocation lines are kept as text reconstructed from
  the preprocessed tokens (blanks preserved, PARSE_FLAG_SPACES; strings
  as written so that "\@" survives): "\op\()_safe_regs" and tokens
  pasted with ## stay glued.  Arguments are split like GNU as: blanks
  or commas, not inside quotes or parentheses, quotes removed
  (ALTERNATIVE "jmp x", "", FEATURE); keyword arguments name=value;
  parameters with :req, :vararg and =default (also defaults such as
  ALT_NOT(X86_FEATURE_ALWAYS)); .exitm; .irpc; .rept re-done on text.
* Conditionals: .elseif, .ifdef/.ifndef, .ifb/.ifnb, .ifeq/.ifne/
  .ifge/.ifgt/.ifle/.iflt, .ifeqs/.ifnes, with proper nesting while a
  false branch is skipped.
* .incbin (searched in the -I directories too), .comm/.lcomm, .local,
  .zero, .uleb128/.sleb128, .equ/.equiv, .print/.warning/.err, .loc,
  .altmacro/.noaltmacro, .protected/.internal; .cfi_* are ignored;
  ".type name STT_FUNC" without the comma (SYM_FUNC_END).
* .section: the flags spelled out replace the defaults, which now
  depend on the name as in GNU as (an unknown name gives no flags),
  and the @nobits/@note type is honoured (the kernel's .pgtable).
* .byte/.word with symbols emit 8/16-bit relocations (R_X86_64_8/16,
  R_386_8/16, the PC-relative ones for "sym - .").
* Expressions: registers compare by identity (".if \base == %rsp" in
  the unwind hints); C suffixes on numbers ($0x0700a169U).
* A whole file is assembled twice when it subtracts labels defined
  later (the .skip of the ALTERNATIVE macros), like inline asm already
  was: tccpp's new preprocess_restart() re-reads the file keeping the
  token table and the symbols but dropping the file's #defines and the
  include-once cache.
* tccpp: the type-size macros (__CHAR_BIT__, __SIZEOF_INT__, __LP64__
  ...) are predefined for assembler files too (asm-generic/bitsperlong.h
  checks them); a ## paste that does not form one token keeps the text
  glued without a warning in an asm file, like cpp.

Verified: all x86_64 .S files of the tinyconfig kernel assemble except
those needing .code32/.code16 switching or AVX; make test passes.

